parameters.content:
## 🔌 Step 4: Connect this MCP server to Claude

Option A — claude.ai / Claude Desktop / Claude Mobile (GUI)
1. Go to Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector
2. Paste your n8n MCP webhook URL (from the MCP Server Trigger node)
3. Open "Advanced settings" → Request headers (beta feature — may need enabling)
4. Add header:
   Name: Authorization
   Value: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE
5. Click Add, then enable it for your chat via the "+" → Connectors menu

Option B — Claude Code (CLI), exact JSON to paste into .mcp.json:

{
  "mcpServers": {
    "blogger-mcp": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "YOUR_N8N_MCP_WEBHOOK_URL",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE"
      }
    }
  }
}

Or via terminal command instead of editing the file:
claude mcp add --transport http blogger-mcp YOUR_N8N_MCP_WEBHOOK_URL --header "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE"

⚠️ Replace YOUR_N8N_MCP_WEBHOOK_URL with your MCP Server Trigger's Production URL, and YOUR_TOKEN_HERE with the Bearer Auth token you set in n8n credentials.

